  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1035 PM CDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nFor the last few nights, models weren't quite sure what to do with \nthis ridge. The picture became a little clearer last night and I \nthink we're tracking right towards a decent heat wave by the end of \nthe week. For the last two runs, the NBM has increased temperatures \na degree or two each day through Sunday, culminating with triple \ndigits in several spots Sunday afternoon. Now, what I know that the \nNBM doesn't is that BNA doesn't hit triple digits very often. \nHowever, even 98-99 degrees is going to be miserable and even if\nBNA doesn't get there, there will several that do. Here's the \nkicker -- NBM probs of seeing triple digits on Saturday or \nSunday? 80%. Yeah, it's going to be a miserable week. The good \nnews, the more of this ridge axis we get, the less the \nthunderstorm coverage should be. I don't know if that's a glass \nhalf-full way of looking at it. This guy already hates summer. So,\nif you know people who are sensitive to heat, you may want to \nstart making plans to keep an eye on them for the rest of this \nweek and into next weekend.",
